And now you see the application
running in the browser.

00:25:20.270 --> 00:25:21.400
I can create a task.

00:25:23.759 --> 00:25:24.550
This is the pop-up.

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:30.940
I gave it just a title, just
from data, and a task date.

00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:33.820
You see, you get a
nice date component.

00:25:33.820 --> 00:25:35.110
I submit it.

00:25:35.110 --> 00:25:37.490
And once it's there,
I can select it.

00:25:37.490 --> 00:25:40.420
And then I can also
flag it as completed.

00:25:40.420 --> 00:25:42.610
And once I completed it,
you see that it is also

00:25:42.610 --> 00:25:43.980
completed in the top.

00:25:46.842 --> 00:25:49.230
All right.

00:25:49.230 --> 00:25:57.680
OK, so what you've seen is I
didn't use any coding here.

00:25:57.680 --> 00:25:59.990
I was just dragging
and dropping.

00:25:59.990 --> 00:26:03.080
But if I wanted to
make it more advanced,

00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:06.260
I could use some coding.

00:26:06.260 --> 00:26:08.810
You just need some JavaScript
knowledge for that.

00:26:08.810 --> 00:26:11.660
That can be JavaScript on
the client, in the browser.

00:26:11.660 --> 00:26:13.700
So then you just write
normal JavaScript code.

00:26:13.700 --> 00:26:17.090
Or it can be App script code.

00:26:17.090 --> 00:26:20.450
But you add that code in
the Apps script itself.

00:26:20.450 --> 00:26:24.470
And automatically, you make
use of all the Google APIs,

00:26:24.470 --> 00:26:26.640
and you can start
playing around with that.

00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:34.170
So App Maker will
be available in Q4.

00:26:34.170 --> 00:26:36.360
If you want, you can start
playing around with it.

00:26:36.360 --> 00:26:39.007
You need to be a G
Suite business customer.

00:26:39.007 --> 00:26:41.340
You can go to this page and
you can write this yourself.

00:26:41.340 --> 00:26:43.800
So you can start
playing around with it.

00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:46.590
I definitely would advise
you to play around with it,

00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:51.180
because it's so easy to create
an application nowadays.

00:26:51.180 --> 00:26:54.960
And with that, I'd like to
hand it over to Leo Koster,

00:26:54.960 --> 00:27:00.900
from VOGSY, who has a
business application created.

00:27:00.900 --> 00:27:02.900
And he likes to talk about that.

00:27:02.900 --> 00:27:03.616
So thank you.

00:27:03.616 --> 00:27:05.480
[APPLAUSE]

00:27:08.105 --> 00:27:09.230
LEO KOSTER: Thank you, Lee.

00:27:12.300 --> 00:27:14.880
Hi, I'm Leo Koster.

00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:17.940
I own an enterprise
software company

00:27:17.940 --> 00:27:22.950
that is successful in
business since 1987.

00:27:22.950 --> 00:27:25.680
And we were one of
the first in Holland

00:27:25.680 --> 00:27:30.800
to be available on the
internet, online, in 2001.

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:32.730
But I wasn't happy.

00:27:32.730 --> 00:27:36.090
Some three years ago, I
realized that we were not

00:27:36.090 --> 00:27:39.510
moving fast enough, not
innovating hard enough,

00:27:39.510 --> 00:27:42.660
not preparing ourselves
for future challenges.

00:27:42.660 --> 00:27:45.180
And I asked myself,
what is happening?

00:27:45.180 --> 00:27:46.800
The world is changing.

00:27:46.800 --> 00:27:48.850
And software is
eating the world.

00:27:48.850 --> 00:27:53.000
It's about new customers asking
me questions I couldn't answer.

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:55.560
And I saw a new
type of employees

00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:58.790
coming that were
switching from software

00:27:58.790 --> 00:28:04.470
their boss taught them to use
to software they love using.

00:28:04.470 --> 00:28:07.560
And that became our new
mission, to create software

00:28:07.560 --> 00:28:10.980
for the business
user that they love.

00:28:10.980 --> 00:28:15.570
And to be able to
deliver on that promise,

00:28:15.570 --> 00:28:19.650
we had to create something
completely new, from scratch.

00:28:19.650 --> 00:28:21.630
And that is VOGSY.

00:28:24.850 --> 00:28:27.710
VOGSY solves one problem.

00:28:27.710 --> 00:28:29.020
Let me give you an example.

00:28:29.020 --> 00:28:31.450
You're an IT services company.

00:28:31.450 --> 00:28:33.130
And you're successful.

00:28:33.130 --> 00:28:34.120
And you're growing.

00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:36.580
The first thing
you put into place

00:28:36.580 --> 00:28:40.000
is something on the back
end for a financial solution

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:43.960
to take care of your invoicing
and cache collection.

00:28:43.960 --> 00:28:47.050
And then you go over to
putting something into place

00:28:47.050 --> 00:28:50.380
to attract customers
and keep them--

00:28:50.380 --> 00:28:52.750
outbound-inbound marketing.

00:28:52.750 --> 00:28:56.380
But in the middle, it's chaos.

00:28:56.380 --> 00:29:00.820
It's a combination of different
apps, custom solutions, paper,

00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:02.280
you name it.

00:29:02.280 --> 00:29:04.975
VOGSY turns this into a
smooth and efficient process.

00:29:07.530 --> 00:29:10.350
Why business apps?

00:29:10.350 --> 00:29:13.170
Let me introduce to
you Willem, Willem

00:29:13.170 --> 00:29:19.260
[? Loesch, ?] founder and CEO of
one of our launching customers.

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:25.050
Willem's job is to produce one
of Holland's most famous export

00:29:25.050 --> 00:29:26.640
products--

00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:27.890
parties.

00:29:27.890 --> 00:29:33.090
They started out by producing
the shows of DJ Chesto.

00:29:33.090 --> 00:29:39.630
Now, they're producing big
corporate events worldwide.

00:29:39.630 --> 00:29:45.340
And with every event, they
produce tons of information--

00:29:45.340 --> 00:29:48.930
project planning, resource
planning, rigging planning,

00:29:48.930 --> 00:29:54.870
sound planning, light planning,
sketches, detailed schemas--

00:29:54.870 --> 00:29:57.480
massive amounts of data.

00:29:57.480 --> 00:30:01.590
And they share this with
hundreds of people--

00:30:01.590 --> 00:30:06.690
temporary employees, customers,
contractors, subcontractors--

00:30:06.690 --> 00:30:07.740
everybody.

00:30:07.740 --> 00:30:10.950
Everybody is connected
and working together,

00:30:10.950 --> 00:30:13.530
collaborating on G Suite.

00:30:13.530 --> 00:30:18.020
And G Suite enabled Willem
to grow even further.

00:30:18.020 --> 00:30:20.610
But Willem was
missing something.

00:30:20.610 --> 00:30:23.460
Willem came to us
with a question.

00:30:23.460 --> 00:30:27.120
Why can't I find a
business app that

00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:29.100
is integrating all
that information

00:30:29.100 --> 00:30:34.290
from G Suite into something
I can look at at my phone?

00:30:34.290 --> 00:30:35.370
Why?

00:30:35.370 --> 00:30:39.630
Because when Willem is
producing his events worldwide,

00:30:39.630 --> 00:30:42.700
this is his office, a taxi--

00:30:42.700 --> 00:30:45.010
and in this case,
a taxi in Tokyo.

00:30:45.010 --> 00:30:46.740
The backseat of the
taxi is his office.

00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:49.420
And he wants to be able
to sit there and have

00:30:49.420 --> 00:30:52.420
a look at his phone and to
see whether his projects are

00:30:52.420 --> 00:30:57.280
on track, his people productive,
his invoices going out,

00:30:57.280 --> 00:30:59.830
and the money coming in.

00:30:59.830 --> 00:31:02.380
And of course, we told
him, look no further.

00:31:02.380 --> 00:31:04.060
We have VOGSY.

00:31:04.060 --> 00:31:05.890
What is VOGSY?

00:31:05.890 --> 00:31:11.180
VOGSY is a vertical solution
for a very specific market.

00:31:11.180 --> 00:31:13.420
It's for professional services.

00:31:13.420 --> 00:31:16.660
It's for everybody who
is delivering services

00:31:16.660 --> 00:31:19.540
through projects with
highly-skilled professionals

00:31:19.540 --> 00:31:20.140
on the move.

00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:26.160
What sets VOGSY apart--

00:31:26.160 --> 00:31:29.030
that's three things.

00:31:29.030 --> 00:31:31.900
The first one-- it's a
social user experience.

00:31:31.900 --> 00:31:35.800
We've taken the best
examples of social media

00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:37.330
to the business space.

00:31:37.330 --> 00:31:41.290
We've taken the timeline the
activity stream to the business

00:31:41.290 --> 00:31:43.510
user.

00:31:43.510 --> 00:31:44.830
And how's that helping?

00:31:44.830 --> 00:31:49.090
Because then nobody has to ask
anymore, where can I find it?

00:31:49.090 --> 00:31:53.680
--the most commonly asked
question with business users.

00:31:53.680 --> 00:31:57.040
And we have an avatar with
VOGSY-- that's Victor--

00:31:57.040 --> 00:31:59.950
who's helping you
through the day.

00:31:59.950 --> 00:32:02.410
Mobile first-- that's obvious.

00:32:02.410 --> 00:32:04.090
Because in a couple
of years, there

00:32:04.090 --> 00:32:05.650
won't be any more mobile first.

00:32:05.650 --> 00:32:07.900
It will be mobile only.

00:32:07.900 --> 00:32:10.600
And the third one
is a no-brainer,

00:32:10.600 --> 00:32:14.200
because Google Cloud will
be the dominant platform

00:32:14.200 --> 00:32:17.140
with next generations.

00:32:17.140 --> 00:32:19.480
Who is using VOGSY?

00:32:19.480 --> 00:32:23.290
The account manager responsible
for the customer, the project

00:32:23.290 --> 00:32:28.360
manager responsible for the
projects, the professional,

00:32:28.360 --> 00:32:31.900
the engineer,
consultant, developer

00:32:31.900 --> 00:32:36.730
doing the actual job, the
manager, and the support

00:32:36.730 --> 00:32:39.160
staff in the back office.

00:32:39.160 --> 00:32:40.570
And how are they
working together

00:32:40.570 --> 00:32:43.310
in this quote to cash process?

00:32:43.310 --> 00:32:44.770
It goes like that.

00:32:44.770 --> 00:32:47.860
It starts with the account
manager creating the quote.

00:32:47.860 --> 00:32:49.900
Then it goes through
the organization.

00:32:49.900 --> 00:32:54.300
And it's a pretty
straightforward process.

00:32:54.300 --> 00:32:59.190
It's expensive-- in the
purchase invoices going out.

00:32:59.190 --> 00:33:02.872
And oh, let me go back.

00:33:02.872 --> 00:33:07.430
Oop, I'm too fast here.

00:33:07.430 --> 00:33:11.530
And then, if you do this
a multitude of times, then

00:33:11.530 --> 00:33:13.930
perhaps it can be handy
to have a manager around

00:33:13.930 --> 00:33:16.400
to have some overview.

00:33:16.400 --> 00:33:22.090
And the crucial thing
here is the handovers.

00:33:22.090 --> 00:33:25.270
I need to have my information
at exactly the right time

00:33:25.270 --> 00:33:26.260
to do my job.

00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:29.050
It's the handover between all
those personas, those roles

00:33:29.050 --> 00:33:30.200
in professional services.

00:33:32.710 --> 00:33:34.990
And VOGSY turns this
into a smooth, speedy,

00:33:34.990 --> 00:33:37.930
and efficient process.

00:33:37.930 --> 00:33:39.290
And how did we do that?

00:33:39.290 --> 00:33:42.220
How did we develop VOGSY?

00:33:42.220 --> 00:33:46.400
When we knew we had
to start from scratch,

00:33:46.400 --> 00:33:49.630
I started looking at what
other successful software

00:33:49.630 --> 00:33:51.310
companies were doing.

00:33:51.310 --> 00:33:55.060
And they were making use of
other people's hard work.

00:33:55.060 --> 00:33:58.140
They were using platforms,
platforms as a surface.

00:33:58.140 --> 00:34:01.840
And I made an inventory of
all the available platforms.

00:34:01.840 --> 00:34:05.740
And for me, the most
innovative, the most fun,

00:34:05.740 --> 00:34:08.560
the most technologically
advanced,

00:34:08.560 --> 00:34:11.139
was the Google Cloud platform.

00:34:11.139 --> 00:34:12.760
And it gave me all
the possibilities

00:34:12.760 --> 00:34:15.730
to create something beautiful.

00:34:15.730 --> 00:34:18.830
And we formulated
some starting points--

00:34:18.830 --> 00:34:21.110
do as little as possible.

00:34:21.110 --> 00:34:22.600
Use what is
available, because you

00:34:22.600 --> 00:34:26.110
want to be able to put a
minimum viable product out

00:34:26.110 --> 00:34:29.620
on the market with as little
effort as possible and as soon

00:34:29.620 --> 00:34:31.909
as possible.

00:34:31.909 --> 00:34:35.510
Use everything by Google,
managed by Google.

00:34:35.510 --> 00:34:36.460
We are developers.

00:34:36.460 --> 00:34:40.120
So even DevOps is
difficult for us.

00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:42.714
We want to develop no ops.

00:34:42.714 --> 00:34:43.739
Oh, sorry.

00:34:43.739 --> 00:34:46.780
Let's go back.

00:34:46.780 --> 00:34:50.050
Building something new
for this connected world

00:34:50.050 --> 00:34:52.150
makes only sense if you
have a global ambition.

00:34:52.150 --> 00:34:54.610
So skill is important.

00:34:54.610 --> 00:34:57.370
Design for scalability.

00:34:57.370 --> 00:34:59.560
And for the business
user, security

00:34:59.560 --> 00:35:02.820
is of paramount importance.

00:35:02.820 --> 00:35:05.680
And with Google Cloud
Platform and working together

00:35:05.680 --> 00:35:08.050
with G Suite, we
get that security.

00:35:10.980 --> 00:35:12.780
Being on the Google
Cloud Platform

00:35:12.780 --> 00:35:16.050
allows us to have a very
clean and simple architecture.

00:35:16.050 --> 00:35:19.270
And we love clean and simple.

00:35:19.270 --> 00:35:23.550
We have Angular on the front
end, Python on the back end,

00:35:23.550 --> 00:35:26.190
all managed by
Google on App Engine.

00:35:26.190 --> 00:35:30.690
And the data is stored
in the Cloud Datastore--

00:35:30.690 --> 00:35:31.860
nothing more.

00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:34.230
Simple.

00:35:34.230 --> 00:35:37.980
And in our pursuit of no ops, we
use some other Google products.

00:35:37.980 --> 00:35:42.000
Our continuous deployment
is fully automated.

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:44.400
With Jenkins on
Compute Engine, we

00:35:44.400 --> 00:35:49.200
monitor VOGSY by using Google
Analytics and the combination

00:35:49.200 --> 00:35:51.900
of Stackdriver and BigQuery.

00:35:51.900 --> 00:35:56.070
And we slice and
dice the information

00:35:56.070 --> 00:36:00.360
with streaming the
data to BigQuery

00:36:00.360 --> 00:36:04.310
and analyzing it
with Data Studio.

00:36:04.310 --> 00:36:07.476
Here are some examples of
the integration with G Suite.

00:36:07.476 --> 00:36:10.470
The first one-- it's
user management,

00:36:10.470 --> 00:36:12.120
identity management.

00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:14.100
Every user, especially
the business user,

00:36:14.100 --> 00:36:16.860
hates logging on,
signing in, especially

00:36:16.860 --> 00:36:20.370
if they have to sign in
to different applications

00:36:20.370 --> 00:36:22.910
to complete one job.

00:36:22.910 --> 00:36:27.750
And we've taken care of that
by using the Google account.

00:36:27.750 --> 00:36:31.374
It's a matter of signing in,
choose the right account,

00:36:31.374 --> 00:36:32.040
and you're done.

00:36:35.410 --> 00:36:37.510
Another example is storing data.

00:36:37.510 --> 00:36:39.240
Everybody knows
how difficult it is

00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:43.170
to get users to store the
data with the right projects,

00:36:43.170 --> 00:36:45.720
right customers,
right opportunities.

00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:49.890
We provide them with this little
icon, this little button here.

00:36:49.890 --> 00:36:54.375
And you click it and you go
exactly to the right folder,

00:36:54.375 --> 00:36:55.980
all managed through
the right APIs.

00:37:01.190 --> 00:37:04.670
Everybody knows that
account managers

00:37:04.670 --> 00:37:08.840
love to copy old quotes and
edit them-- copy and paste.

00:37:08.840 --> 00:37:11.420
And I'm not going into
details about all the problems

00:37:11.420 --> 00:37:13.340
that it's creating.

00:37:13.340 --> 00:37:17.210
So we've made it easy for
them to just click one button,

00:37:17.210 --> 00:37:19.310
create a new quote.

00:37:19.310 --> 00:37:23.570
And it is created with the right
template, the right settings,

00:37:23.570 --> 00:37:27.060
in the right folder, and is
ready there for them to edit.

00:37:29.570 --> 00:37:31.470
This is one of my favorites--

00:37:31.470 --> 00:37:32.490
sending out the quote.

00:37:35.610 --> 00:37:38.190
I get notified on my
timeline that it's time

00:37:38.190 --> 00:37:39.750
for me to send out this quote.

00:37:39.750 --> 00:37:42.360
Somebody else approved it.

00:37:42.360 --> 00:37:44.100
I click on the button.

00:37:44.100 --> 00:37:46.890
And it's gone.

00:37:46.890 --> 00:37:49.500
Entering data-- also
some fun points.

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:51.370
Nobody likes to
enter data any more.

00:37:51.370 --> 00:37:52.350
And why should you?

00:37:52.350 --> 00:37:53.190
You're on Google.

00:37:53.190 --> 00:37:56.720
So you have to find information.

00:37:56.720 --> 00:37:58.560
Here, I'm creating
a new organization

00:37:58.560 --> 00:38:01.530
with a contact person.

00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:04.770
I am looking up the
right organization

00:38:04.770 --> 00:38:06.950
through the Google Places API.

00:38:06.950 --> 00:38:08.400
Select it.

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:13.350
Select the right contact,
through a plus API.

00:38:13.350 --> 00:38:16.980
And when I've entered
them, the result

00:38:16.980 --> 00:38:19.920
is a cart filled with
the contact information,

00:38:19.920 --> 00:38:21.600
the right pictures, logos.

00:38:21.600 --> 00:38:22.100
I'm done.

00:38:24.690 --> 00:38:29.440
Management and support staff--
they love Sheets for reporting.

00:38:29.440 --> 00:38:33.360
So we created a bunch
of sheets for them.

00:38:33.360 --> 00:38:38.100
And here you have a
financial example.

00:38:38.100 --> 00:38:42.390
And table, Sheets, easy to use.

00:38:42.390 --> 00:38:45.600
And we've developed their
own add-on with Apps Script

00:38:45.600 --> 00:38:51.000
to refresh the data
into that report.

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:54.600
And last but not
least, installing VOGSY

00:38:54.600 --> 00:38:58.260
through G Suite Marketplace--

00:38:58.260 --> 00:39:01.340
we're using that
API to get VOGSY--

00:39:01.340 --> 00:39:07.440
oh, sorry, let me get it back--

00:39:07.440 --> 00:39:10.530
to get VOGSY into
your own domain

00:39:10.530 --> 00:39:14.400
with all the right settings
for the right users.

00:39:14.400 --> 00:39:17.490
That was the last example.

00:39:17.490 --> 00:39:19.260
Curious about VOGSY?

00:39:19.260 --> 00:39:22.440
We have a booth there
in the main hall.

00:39:22.440 --> 00:39:26.570
If you have any
questions, please ask us.

00:39:26.570 --> 00:39:27.778
LEE BOONSTRA: Thank you, Leo.

00:39:27.778 --> 00:39:29.242
[APPLAUSE]

00:39:30.146 --> 00:39:30.770
Thank you, Leo.

00:39:30.770 --> 00:39:32.720
It's pretty impressive,
that application.

00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:36.070
So definitely visit
the VOGSY booth.

00:39:36.070 --> 00:39:38.920
So now you have seen there
are various ways in how

00:39:38.920 --> 00:39:40.302
you can create applications.

00:39:40.302 --> 00:39:42.230
Hey, you can do that
through App script.

00:39:42.230 --> 00:39:44.680
You can do that with
your own codebase

00:39:44.680 --> 00:39:48.010
and just integrate the
Google APIs inside of that.

00:39:48.010 --> 00:39:50.230
Or you can App Maker.

00:39:50.230 --> 00:39:53.410
And with that, I would like
to thank you for being here

00:39:53.410 --> 00:39:55.010
and wish you a very great day.

00:39:55.010 --> 00:39:56.801
And I don't want to
keep you up from lunch.

00:39:56.801 --> 00:39:57.940
So thank you very much.

00:39:57.940 --> 00:40:00.090
[APPLAUSE]

